      "side": 1,
      "message": "This happens with any AIDL IGnss HAL implementation that does not support one or more of the five optional extensions and returns Status::ok() with a null binder (we hit it with our AIDL IGnss wrapper backed by a MediaTek HIDL 2.1 GNSS HAL that lacks some optional extensions).\n\nIn hardware/interfaces/gnss/aidl/android/hardware/gnss/IGnss.aidl, exactly those five getters are annotated @nullable:\n- getExtensionPsds() (line 146)\n- getExtensionGnssBatching() (line 180)\n- getExtensionGnssGeofence() (line 187)\n- getExtensionGnssNavigationMessage() (line 194)\n- getExtensionMeasurementCorrections() (line 334)\n\nReturning Status::ok() with nullptr is therefore explicitly valid per the AIDL contract (and mirrors the HIDL branches right below in Gnss.cpp, where checkHidlReturn() already verifies both isOk() and non-null before wrapping). Without the nullptr check, Gnss.cpp wraps the null sp\u003c\u003e and system_server crashes on the first dereference.",
